  "version": "0.10.17",
  "description": "Adds Shen and reworks official champions 002-007 and 009 as Lucian, Orianna, Briar, Sivir, Kled, Xayah and Yone. Version 0.10.17 targets Teamfight Manager 2 base 0.5.1 and uses the matching official 0.5.1 SDK. Version 0.10.16 is retained as a failed Yone portrait-layout route: it correctly discovered the shared UI NinePatch source at 95x88, but expanded that command to the portrait PNG's 90x122 canvas and therefore also enlarged and lowered Yone on the post-pick player-assignment page. The default 0.10.17 Yone-only extension distinguishes the real swap container from the central champion viewport, keeps each original 95x88 command's width and height, preserves x everywhere, and samples only the top 88 of the existing 90x122 dual_blader_grid PNG. The central grid also preserves y; assignment and edge pick cards move y upward by 9 logical pixels to restore bottom clearance without changing the accepted face, body, legs, boots or portrait asset. The 85x93 management, compact and scoreboard routes remain independent; Game-pass RenderCommand::Sprite battle actors and other champions cannot match. Bounded telemetry now records surface, UI root, command coordinates, output coordinates and normalized UV so reused 95x88 components remain distinguishable. No Yone actor, portrait, skill, VFX, icon or audio asset is changed. V6 keeps the official 3502x88 battle canvas, 13 animation tags, rectangles, labels and timings; Q/W/R gameplay and the saved-season floor introduced in 0.10.5 remain unchanged. A save first created on 0.10.5 or later remains valid. Spirit Cleave still performs one stateless 80-degree, 42000-range GameCtx cone scan with no process-global ledger, deals 35 + 45% Attack + 6% target maximum-health physical damage, and settles one shield tier for zero through five champions hit; Mod API 0.8 still requires fixed 0.5-second cast and 8-second cooldown. Retired E and 0.10.4 rectangular-W native names remain no-op saved-data compatibility only so old embedded trees do not crash after BP. The broader legacy MatchUIRunner, ClientDatabase, picked-side splash, dragon, server and other-champion rewrites remain explicitly opt-in. Automated source and build checks do not constitute live visual acceptance; the 0.10.17 route remains pending in-game user verification.",
  "last_updated": "2026-07-22",
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "mod_id": "base",
      "version": ">=0.5.1"
    }
  ]
}
